cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or the accompanying dataset, please cite the original
  paper listed under "references" and this repository.

title: >-
  Liquid-crystal skyrmion CNN analysis: physical simulation, POM dataset
  engineering, and CNN-based parameter inversion

abstract: >-
  Reproduction of the methodology of Terroa, Tasinkevych & Dias (Scientific
  Reports 15:10921, 2025) for liquid-crystal skyrmions. This branch (roleB)
  contains the convolutional neural network pipeline with three Keras
  architectures that invert polarised optical microscopy (POM) textures into
  pitch, applied voltage and free energy across seven classification /
  regression tasks. The companion physical-simulation and dataset-generation
  pipeline (968 grayscale 300x300 POM images with pitch, voltage and
  Frank-Oseen free-energy labels) is maintained on the roleA branch of the
  same repository.

type: software

authors:
  # 建议在此填入两位成员的真实姓名（CFF 允许 person 条目，含 family-names / given-names）。
  # 当前使用项目实体名，避免误填。
  - name: "Undergraduate Innovation and Entrepreneurship Training Program — Nematic Liquid Crystal Topological Defects Project"

